{
  "name": "AI Revenue OS - Combined (3 flows, 1 file)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "92ab116e-7edf-4213-8b31-4653ad943d74",
      "name": "Note: Combined AI Revenue OS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "AI REVENUE OS -- 3 workflows, 1 file\n\nThis single file contains three independent flows, each with its own webhook trigger, stacked top-to-bottom:\n\n  Lane 1 (y ~ -420 to 200):   LEAD -> OUTREACH\n  Lane 2 (y ~ 780 to 1400):   LEAD -> APPOINTMENT\n  Lane 3 (y ~ 1980 to 2600):  APPOINTMENT -> REVENUE\n\nThey are NOT chained to each other inside this file -- each is triggered by its own webhook (lead-intake / inbound-message / trigger-proposal) exactly as when they were 3 separate files. Call workflow 3's webhook from wherever a lead becomes QUALIFIED/APPOINTMENT (e.g. from your CRM, or add an HTTP Request node at the end of Lane 2 pointing at Lane 3's webhook URL once imported). 38 functional nodes total, same as the 3-file version -- only the packaging changed.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fff1ff56-448d-487f-8b09-5b9c828ad09e",
      "name": "Note: LEAD -> OUTREACH\n\nWe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "LEAD -> OUTREACH\n\nWebhook -> Validate -> Research -> Groq Score -> Save -> Groq Outreach -> Human Approval (Wait node, resumes on webhook call) -> Gmail -> Update CRM.\n\nReliability: retryOnFail on both HTTP calls (transient errors), graceful score fallback on malformed AI JSON (application errors) -- no separate retry sub-flow needed for a single-purpose workflow this size.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f8090651-2747-4cc3-a380-0c98a2badc94",
      "name": "[1 LEAD->OUTREACH] Webhook - Lead Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "76515e57-5f1b-4d0b-b276-68972af19761",
      "name": "[1 LEAD->OUTREACH] Validate + Sanitize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const item = ($input.first().json.body) || $input.first().json;\nconst errors = [];\nconst emailRe = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\nfunction clean(v){ if(typeof v !== 'string') return v; return v.replace(/<[^>]*>/g,'').trim().slice(0,2000); }\nconst name = clean(item.name), email = clean(item.email||''), phone = clean(item.phone||'');\nif(!name) errors.push('missing_name');\nif(!email && !phone) errors.push('missing_contact');\nif(email && !emailRe.test(email)) errors.push('invalid_email');\nreturn [{ json: {\n  valid: errors.length === 0, errors,\n  lead_id: 'lead_' + Date.now().toString(36) + '_' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2,8),\n  name, email: email.toLowerCase(), phone, company: clean(item.company||''), website: clean(item.website||''),\n  message: clean(item.message||''), service: clean(item.service||''), budget: clean(item.budget||''),\n  source: clean(item.source||'unknown'), created_at: new Date().toISOString(), status: 'NEW', deal_stage: 'NEW'\n}}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9990d901-7b1c-4a45-88c3-f452f4b9bebd",
      "name": "[1 LEAD->OUTREACH] IF - Valid",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{$json.valid}}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      }
    },
